# Single source of truth for TEST database credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env.test` (or source directly) and make sure ALL of the
# following read from here, instead of hard-coding their own values:
#   - Makefile (start-db / wait-db / migrate targets)
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml (postgres service env + migration step)
#   - test fixtures / conftest that set POSTGRES_* env vars at import time
#
# Lesson learned: a real project had three different places hard-coding
# mismatched credentials (tests expected "alfred_api/topicsdb", Makefile
# and CI both created "postgres/postgres"), causing test runs to hang
# while retrying the DB connection. Keeping ONE file as the source of
# truth prevents that class of bug.

POSTGRES_USER=app_test
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=test-password
POSTGRES_DB=app_testdb
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
